# Copy to .env before the first `docker compose up`. Compose reads it
# automatically and the file is git-ignored, so real values never leave the
# host. Every variable below has a working default except the database
# password, which is required on purpose.

# --- required --------------------------------------------------------------

# Password for the bundled Postgres container. Anything works for a local try;
# generate a real one for an instance anybody else can reach.
CAL_DB_PASSWORD=change-me


# --- optional: the database ------------------------------------------------
# CAL_DB_NAME=calendar
# CAL_DB_USER=calendar
# CAL_TZ=America/New_York


# --- optional: the login (a public-internet front door) ---------------------
# Leave both empty for a private-network-only run: loopback, RFC1918 and
# Tailscale-range addresses are trusted and never see a login screen, because
# being on the private network is already the proof. Without these set, a
# visitor arriving from anywhere else is refused rather than prompted, which
# is the safe direction to fail.
#
# CAL_GATE_SECRET is the HMAC key for the session cookie: any long random
# string (`openssl rand -hex 32`). CAL_GATE_USERS is a comma separated list of
# name=hash pairs. Mint a hash with
#   python app/gate.py 'the-password'
# and paste the whole pbkdf2:... string. Plain passwords never go in here.
# CAL_GATE_SECRET=
# CAL_GATE_USERS=willian=pbkdf2:600000:1a2b3c...:9f8e7d...,aline=pbkdf2:600000:...:...


# --- optional: who is holding the device -------------------------------------
# Maps a device's private-network address to a person, purely so it can show
# that person's own background pictures with no login involved. /who in the
# app reports the address it actually saw for a device that is not yet
# mapped. Unset means every device sees the shared pictures.
# CAL_DEVICES=100.101.102.1=willian,100.101.102.2=aline


# --- optional: Telegram reminders --------------------------------------------
# Both unset simply means the reminder loop never starts, and the app says so
# once at startup: no reminders, no crash. Token from @BotFather; chats as
# Name=id pairs whose names MUST match the event owner values (Willian,
# Aline), because reminders route on the event's owner field.
# CAL_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
# CAL_TELEGRAM_CHATS=Willian=111111111,Aline=222222222


# --- optional: the "what's on" rail ------------------------------------------
# Free key from https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api. Without it the rail
# says so plainly and everything else works unchanged.
# CAL_TMDB_KEY=


# --- optional: the portal link -----------------------------------------------
# Where the header's 🏠 icon points when this app is reached on its own port.
# Empty means there is no portal to go back to and the icon is not drawn.
# When the app is served under a path prefix (X-Forwarded-Prefix) the icon
# points at that host's root instead and this value is ignored.
# CAL_PORTAL_URL=


# --- optional: the create-reminder API (the finances app) -------------------
# Shared bearer key for POST /api/reminders. Leave unset and the endpoint
# 503s for everyone rather than opening up: there is no login on the
# private-network path, so this key is the only guard. Any long random
# string (`openssl rand -hex 32`); the finances app sends it as
# `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
# CAL_API_KEY=
